{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>עוצה</b> — In my opinion, that he shuts their eyes. עוצם עיניו — they are from the root עוצה עיניו, and the mem is a sign of the [hollow] verbs, and the proper form is עוצה אותם את עיניהם. Similarly, ותפתח ותראהו את הילד — לחללו את ביתו, the correct form is לחלל אותו. And likewise the interpretation: עוצה עיניו — he shuts his eyes, so that his heart will not go after his eyes, because he plots reversals as he wills." "<b>כלה</b> — brings the evil to completion, as he planned."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The comment appears to discuss the root עצם/עוץ and conjugation patterns; the syntax of the grammatical argument is compressed and the exact force of 'המ״ם סימן הפועלים' is ambiguous — translated literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:17.853981635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}